Engine half of the duplicate fix (src/pushwatch.ts)

Every alert now carries a TRANSITION SIGNATURE — the identity that survives a
re-derivation, which the card's text cannot provide (it carries live numbers).
The rules engine also learns the two things that let a re-derived card be
recognised as a duplicate: a cut-card mark read off the row's own mark CSV, and
the audit-derived delivery proof. And the 🚀 memory walk marks every crossed
stage instead of one per cooldown window, which is what turned a single gap into
five near-identical POPEYE cards.

Apply BEFORE cut-card-dedupe.patch (which wires the tracker side).

